From: CEB-GNRD maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Use individual authority certificates as the persistent store

The bundle uploaded by InstallAll/ReplaceAll is only a staging input.
Reloading that snapshot after single-certificate CRUD silently revokes
new trust decisions and resurrects certificates deleted by the user.
Discard the snapshot before bulk commit and migrate existing stores to
their individual payloads, including empty stores. Sync acknowledged CA
mutations while preserving bulk staging and rollback. Normal manager
destruction must preserve the canonical CA payloads; explicit deletion
and retired transaction objects continue to remove their files.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board trust-store persistence policy]

